Z||000000||hyhy4u||08-17-2001||11:52 AM||||I searched the cave..and call me stupid but i couldnt find anything on it, lol. So here we go..what does a Accel coil really do..i know it sends more volts through the wires but does that actually do anything..and even more so..do 8mm wires make a difference..i would love to do it just cause it looks cool but if theres really no performacne differece im thinking im spend my money on something else!<P>Thanks..Jason  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||fieronv||08-17-2001||12:10 PM||||I added an Accel coil and 8mm splitfire wires to mine and the biggest difference that I noticed was my idle smoothed out instantly. As for performance I'm not sure but not having a 5 percent misfire from the stock coil has to help. BTW I just drove from Reno to Coos Bay OR. and got 31 MPG with a v6 as good as when my car was brand new. <P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cozmo||08-17-2001||12:14 PM||||The secondary voltage is higher on performance coils (&gt;50KV).  Supposedly the stock coil is only around 35KV.  Also, the aftermarket ones saturate faster, so at high RPMs (&gt;4000) there is more voltage available quicker.  Larger diameter plug wires show less resistance to the coil allowing the plugs to see the full output voltage.  It's critical to have a proper spark plug gap so everything works right.  I just did a MSD system, the biggest improvement I noticed was easier starting and a smoother idle.  If you get the right parts and set them up properly, this is a cheap way of getting a better running and more reliable engine (providing the distributor is OK, but that's a whole subject in itself... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).<BR>BobC||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-17-2001||07:53 PM||||coils for which motor.... The Accell DIS coils are crap. (DIS coils are toward the bottom of my DIS notes article.) Search the forum on Accell and it's various misspellings. I think several people aren't happy with the HEI coil either.<P>Allot of so called performance wires suck. Check out whatever kind you plan to get carefully before you pay for them. I'm putting <A HREF="http://www.magnecor.com/" TARGET=_blank>Magnecor</A> 8mm into mine as soon as the feds get around to sending my tax money. (They are only about $40 for the DIS 4 cyl.) <P>Good ignition parts <u>never</u> add power to an engine but bad ones shure as hell will kill it. If the ignition can't keep up with the rest of the motor the whole package suffers. The performance gains most people feel are power the engine had all along but one or more old ignition parts couldn't deliver.<P>The only reason I'm replacing the Borg Warner wires I got at Pep Boys is that a couple of them are partly rubbed into from being up against something. Those wires are 30,000 miles old and still run perfectly, but I want to get them off before the rubbed sopts start giving me crap. They were only about $25. <P>Keep in mind, I'm talking about a DIS system which by OE design dumps more than twice the power down the wires than HEI does.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||08-17-2001||09:10 PM||||I think many people underestimate the reliability and quality of the GM factory wires. Every aftermarket ignition wire that I have tried was a POS and didn’t last more than 10,000 miles and they would usually leak. I put a set GM wires on and I never have a problem and they last forever. If you’re only going to upgrade to an Accell coil than don’t waste your money on aftermarket junk wires. Get the GM wires. <P>I also personally think the MSD coil is a better coil than the Accell coil. The MSD 6A multiple spark ignition system is also a great upgrade to your ignition system. With the MSD 6A and the MSD coil your engine will never misfire even with worn plugs.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||08-18-2001||01:13 AM||||Accell Supecoils make great paperweights. Mine gave out after 17k miles, but not before degrading both my performance and fuel economy.  Get ANYTHING else.||||reg||1
Z||000006||hyhy4u||08-18-2001||10:16 AM||||After reading what you guys gotta say..im thinking il go with a MSD coil..now where can i get one and how much??||||reg||1
